File:Maedate-shadan Omote-shinmon.JPG|'''Maedate Shrine Platform – Front Shrine Gate'''<br>One of the shrine gates flanking the main hall to the east and west; this is the front shrine gate. The east shrine gate can be seen beyond it.
File:Maedate-shadan Honden.JPG|'''Maedate Shrine Platform – Main Hall'''<br>A structure maintained by powerful figures such as Minamoto no Yoritomo, Ashikaga Yoshitane, and Sassa Narimasa; designated a National {{ill|lt=Important Cultural Property|Q1188622|WD=Q1188622|1=Important Cultural Property (Japan)}} on April 19, {{ill|lt=Meiji|Q3125096|WD=Q3125096|1=Meiji era}} 39 ({{ill|lt=1906|Q2049|WD=Q2049|1=1906}}). The five-bay-wide main hall is said to be the largest in Hokuriku.
