=== Festivals and Rituals ===
* January 1 – New Year’s Day Festival
* January 2 – Beginning of Daily Offerings Festival
* January 3 – {{ill|lt=Genshi-sai|Q11387821|WD=Q11387821|1=Genshi-sai}}
* April 8 – Spring Grand Festival, Mikoshi Procession
* April 29 – Emperor Shōwa Festival
* Auspicious day in June – Prayer for Bountiful Harvest
* June 30 – {{ill|lt=Ōharae|Q11261910|WD=Q11261910|lt=Summer Purification Rite|1=Ōharae-shiki}}
* July 7 – Industry and Traffic Safety Prayer Festival
* July 25 – Mine Main Shrine Festival
* August 21 – Branch Inari Shrine Festival
* August 25 – Branch Hachiman Shrine Festival
* September 15 – Subsidiary Tachi-o Shrine Festival
* November 3 – Autumn Grand Festival ({{ill|lt=Etchū Chigo Dance#Other Toyama Prefecture chigo dances|Q11636372|WD=Q11636372|lt=Chigo Dance|1=Chigo Dance of Etchū}}; Tateyama no Mai ({{ill|lt=Miko dance|Q11479841|WD=Q11479841|1=miko mai}}))
* Auspicious day in November – New Grain Thanksgiving Festival
* December 23 – {{ill|UNKNOWN|lt=Tenchō-sai|1=UNKNOWN}}
* December 31 – Year-End Purification Rite
* December 31 – New Year’s Eve Festival
* Monthly on the 1st – Monthly Festival and Traffic Safety Prayer Festival

=== Cultural Properties ===
=== Important Cultural Properties (National Designation) ===
* Maedate Shrine Platform Main Hall
* Wooden Seated Statue of Monk Jikō

=== Other Items ===
* Autographed manuscript by Emperor Go-Kōmyō
* Folding fan of Emperor Nakamikado
* Crown of Emperor Sakuramachi
* Stone komainu guardian lions
* Boiling cauldron used in divination rites
* Tateyama Mandala paintings
* And many others

=== Transportation Access ===
; Mine Main Shrine
* About a 2-hour mountain climb from {{ill|lt=Murodō Terminal|Q6938821|WD=Q6938821|1=Murodō Station}} on the {{ill|lt=Tateyama Kurobe Alpine Route|Q6425988|WD=Q6425988|1=Tateyama Kurobe Alpine Route}}

; Chūgū Prayer Hall
* From {{ill|lt=Chigaki Station|Q5097198|WD=Q5097198|1=Chigaki Station}} on the {{ill|lt=Toyama Chihō Railway Tateyama Line|Q7830575|WD=Q7830575|lt=Tateyama Line|1=Toyama Chihō Railway Tateyama Line}}, take the Tateyama Town bus (bound for Ashikuraji) and get off at “Oyama Shrine-mae”

; Maedate Shrine Platform
* About a 7-minute walk from {{ill|lt=Iwakuraji Station|Q6100451|WD=Q6100451|1=Iwakuraji Station}} on the {{ill|lt=Toyama Chihō Railway Tateyama Line|Q7830575|WD=Q7830575|lt=Tateyama Line|1=Toyama Chihō Railway Tateyama Line}} and {{ill|lt=Toyama Chihō Railway Kamitaki Line|Q7830572|WD=Q7830572|lt=Kamitaki Line|1=Toyama Chihō Railway Kamidaki Line}}

